<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Senhime</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1597–1666</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sen-hime</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Senhime was a granddaughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> and the eldest daughter of the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-hidetada">Tokugawa Hidetada</a>. Married as a child to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-clan">Toyotomi</a> Hideyori, she was rescued from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka-castle">Osaka Castle</a> when it fell in 1615. She then married Honda Tadatoki, heir of the Honda family that held Himeji, and after his death in 1626 became a Buddhist nun.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/senhime.jpg" alt="Senhime" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 不詳 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Senhime.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
